    "description": "A public road crosses a named creek. Named creeks are usually larger and rise faster in heavy rain. Interstates and US highways are left out. Source: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line 2024 roads and water (creeks from USGS).",
    "color": "#e66101",
    "iconClass": "Circle",
    "popupContentTemplate": "# Creek crosses the road\n**{name}**\n\nIn heavy rain, water can cover the road here.\n\nNever drive into water over a road. Twelve inches of moving water can carry away most cars. Turn around, don't drown."
